- **Shipping a new release** [em dash] section 02 reads `/version.json` before `initialize()` and passes its `build` to `config.cacheVersion`, so a cache built under another release is emptied at boot. Its controls set a new version on the running engine, re-read `version.json`, or call `clearCache()`, beside a live view of the engine's `sessionStorage` keys. Clicking User 7 before and after shows the difference: the progress bar appears only when the fragment is fetched.
- **Validation** [em dash] the buttons in section 03 build throwaway engines to show how `initialize()` refuses an incomplete setup, how `dataAttributeNames`/`classes` reject unknown keys, and how `cacheVersion` rejects an empty value.
